{%- comment -%}
  Rate limits for one authenticated call (spec §12.4): the per-token limit, then the
  per-principal limit.

  The per-token bucket (`principal:<id>:token:<token id>`, defaults.rate_limit_per_min)
  keeps one chatty agent from using up the budget of the person's other agents. The
  per-principal bucket (`principal:<id>`, defaults.rate_limit_per_principal_per_min)
  counts every call the person makes through any of their tokens or OAuth grants, so
  minting more tokens does not raise how fast one person can act.

  The per-principal bucket is bumped only when the per-token check passes, so calls a
  token is already refused for do not use up the person's shared budget.

  Callers count only a "token" refusal as a violation (limits/note_violation): the
  person's other tokens can fill the per-principal bucket, and that must not get the
  calling token auto-suspended.

  @param {string} principal_id
  @param {string} token_id
  @return {object} { allowed, count, limit, retry_after, scope } — scope is "token" or
                   "principal": the limit that answered
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function cfg = 'modules/mcp/helpers/config'
  assign pid = principal_id | append: ''
  assign tid = token_id | append: ''

  assign token_scope = 'principal:' | append: pid | append: ':token:' | append: tid
  function rl = 'modules/mcp/commands/limits/check', scope: token_scope, limit: cfg.defaults.rate_limit_per_min
  assign rl['scope'] = 'token'
  unless rl.allowed
    return rl
  endunless

  assign principal_limit = cfg.defaults.rate_limit_per_principal_per_min | plus: 0
  if principal_limit <= 0
    return rl
  endif

  assign principal_scope = 'principal:' | append: pid
  function prl = 'modules/mcp/commands/limits/check', scope: principal_scope, limit: principal_limit
  assign prl['scope'] = 'principal'
  return prl
%}
